  1701	16A. Ferrari and P. Spoletini
  1702	knowledge graphs can help to constrain the reasoning process, thus
  1703	preventing hallucinations. Secondly, knowledge graphs can provide
  1704	a compact and parsimonious representation of knowledge, which is
  1705	needed when textual information about a domain is not sufficiently
  1706	abundant to train the LLM and can also positively impact efficiency.
  1707	Finally, an external formal knowledge representation can support the
  1708	explainability of the output, as the LLM can resort to a knowledge graph
  1709	not only for retrieving information but also for justifying its content.
  1710	Action Point: Injecting domain-specific knowledge using formal
  1711	ontologies and knowledge graphs can be used to constrain the LLM
  1712	reasoning process, prevent hallucinations, and improve explainability
