   798	control  channel,  and with assertion.
   799	Fig. 1.Counterexample  generated  by Spin when the synchronisation  between  processes
   800	is not in place.
   801	In this version,  the Sender  and Receiver  communicate  without  using
   802	a control  channel.  Since the only communication  channel
   803	(communication ) can buffer up toMAX_MESSAGES messages  (ln 1),
   804	and the Receiver  does not have to wait for a synchronisation  signal,
   805	then the Sender  can continuously  send (and buffer)  messages  (ln 11–
   806	13). The Receiver  can read a message  at any moment  it is available
   807	(ln 24), but because  the Sender  is not bound  to wait for the Receiver
   808	to read before  generating  the new message,  the Sender  could generate
